RECORDED REQUEST CONTEXT (untrusted data; retain frozen obligations):
<<<
Software engineering task G13: Transitive reduction with global cycle checks

Implement solution.py with solve(data). Use only the Python standard library. Do not read files, use the network, print, or retain state across calls. All inputs conform to this specification; return JSON-compatible values. Input {n,edges}, n=0..10, directed [u,v]; duplicates are ignored. Return null if any cycle exists. Otherwise return sorted unique edges [u,v] retained by the DAG transitive reduction: retain an edge exactly when there is no alternate u-to-v path using at least two edges. Preserve reachability, include no redundant edges, and keep isolated vertices implicit.

Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.

Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):
[{"input": {"edges": [[0, 1], [1, 2], [0, 2], [0, 2]], "n": 3}, "output": [[0, 1], [1, 2]]}, {"input": {"edges": [[0, 0]], "n": 1}, "output": null}]

>>>
